/-!
# The paired outside Borel centralizes the original omega orbit

The natural whole-actor coordinates identify the image of the literal
O²(H) action on [U_H,H] with the independent cubic rotations of O₄⁺(2).
Their linear normalizer preserves the quadratic form. Since the original
Borel residual L₁ is two-perfect, its action commutes with those rotations.
The central splitting U_H = [U_H,H] ⊕ C_Z(H), together with [Z,L₁]=1,
then propagates centrality from Z to its entire residual orbit U_H.

When the original Borel join has nontrivial two-core, the proved starred
residual uniqueness supplies the required normalization. Consequently its
omega orbit is still U_H and [L₁,O²(H)] lies in O₂(O²(H)), with all residuals
and cores mapped through their literal subgroup inclusions.

The independent Baumann bound, solvability, faithful-component normalization
and nontrivial join core remain explicit earlier inputs. This is the paired
centrality calculation of 13.2.14, not its s=1 conclusion: the subsequent
13.2.13 contradiction and the remaining original outside argument stay with
qt-d-1367-assembly. The 13.3.2 input retains its existing source owner.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 13.2.8--10 and 13.2.12--14, printed pp.880--883.
-/

